{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started with SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Add the package, build ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"text":" with your token, register the analytics plugin, and start dispatching events.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/gettingstarted"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide is the shortest path from a wired Swidux app with ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" registered to events landing in Mixpanel. It assumes you have already followed Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" guide through Step 5 — that is, your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" has an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" slice, your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":" routes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".analytics(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and you have an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsMapper"},{"type":"text","text":" declared."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add the package","anchor":"Add-the-package","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Xcode:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" File > Add Package Dependencies, paste "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":". Add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},{"text":" product to your target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Package.swift:"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".product(name: \"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\", package: \"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\"),"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Build-the-service-at-launch","text":"Build the service at launch","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" owns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" internally — you do not need to "},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Construct the service with your token (and any Mixpanel knobs you care about) before configuring the store:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","import SwiftUI","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    @State private var store: AppStore","","    init() {","        let analyticsService = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","            token: \"your-mixpanel-token\",","            optOutTrackingByDefault: true","        )","        _store = State(","            wrappedValue: AppStore.configured(","                analyticsService: analyticsService,","                onConsentChange: { await analyticsService.setOptedOut($0) }","            ))","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup { ContentView().environment(store) }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The initializer surfaces every Mixpanel knob the app would otherwise need to set on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"text":" (EU ","type":"text"},{"code":"serverURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flushInterval"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instanceName"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"superProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"useGzipCompression"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackAutomaticEvents"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"excludeProperties"},{"type":"text","text":") and is identical on every platform. Pick what you need; everything else has a sensible default. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the longer treatment.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Register the plugin with `MixpanelAnalyticsService`","anchor":"Register-the-plugin-with-MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass the service to "},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":" factory:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Swidux","import SwiduxAnalytics","import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured(","        analyticsService: some AnalyticsService,","        onConsentChange: (@Sendable (Bool) async -> Void)? = nil","    ) -> AppStore {","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","","        plugins.register(","            AnalyticsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","                state: \\.analytics,","                action: AppAction.analytics,","                extractAction: { if case .analytics(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","                service: analyticsService,","                mapper: analyticsMapper,","                identity: analyticsIdentity,","                onConsentChange: onConsentChange","            )","        )","","        var initialState = AppState()","        initialState.analytics = AnalyticsState(isOptedOut: ConsentStore.isOptedOut)","","        return Store(","            initialState: initialState,","            reducer: AppReducer().reduce,","            plugins: plugins","        )","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That’s it — the plugin will route mapped events through the service, re-fire "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whenever the "},{"code":"(userID, userProperties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pair derived from state changes, and flush on your call to "},{"code":"store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scenePhase == .background"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Keep consent in one place","anchor":"Keep-consent-in-one-place","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut"},{"text":" flag and Mixpanel’s own opt-out must agree. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onConsentChange"},{"text":" keeps them in step whenever the app dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics(.setOptedOut(_:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but the plugin’s flag starts from whatever ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState()"},{"text":" gives it — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" by default — while ","type":"text"},{"code":"optOutTrackingByDefault: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" starts Mixpanel opted out. Left like that, the plugin identifies the user at launch, Mixpanel drops the call, and the plugin never retries it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So keep the user’s consent choice in your own storage ("},{"code":"ConsentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" above stands in for it — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":" is fine), seed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsState(isOptedOut:)"},{"type":"text","text":" from it as shown, and dispatch the stored value once at launch — from your root view’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".task"},{"text":" — so Mixpanel matches it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".task { store.send(.analytics(.setOptedOut(ConsentStore.isOptedOut))) }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Repeating a consent value is harmless: opting in a user who already consented sends nothing, and opting out an opted-out user does nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Verify-the-wiring","text":"Verify the wiring","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dispatch a screen view from your root view’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onAppear"},{"text":" and confirm the event arrives in Mixpanel’s Live View:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        RootContent()","            .onAppear { store.send(.analytics(.screenView(\"Home\"))) }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Next-Steps","text":"Next Steps","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — EU residency, opt-out by default, multiple Mixpanel projects, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelInstance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" escape hatch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — Drive analytics state from previews and tests using ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — How ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" cases map onto Mixpanel "},{"code":"Properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToImplementService":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtoimplementservice","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Configure ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to match your privacy, residency, and batching needs — without ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your app.","type":"text"}],"title":"How to Implement the Service","role":"article"},"https://heirloomlogic.github.io/Swidux/documentation/swidux/howtoaddanalytics":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","title":"Add Analytics","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Analytics"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/Swidux\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"text":" internally so apps never need to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recording "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" for previews and Swift Testing suites.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockmixpanelanalyticsservice"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToPreviewAndTest":{"kind":"article","title":"How to Preview and Test","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites without touching Mixpanel’s network."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtopreviewandtest"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/ValueTranslation":{"kind":"article","title":"Value Translation","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cases map onto Mixpanel’s "},{"code":"MixpanelType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/valuetranslation"}}}